        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(plugins): bound safeHashFile in installed-plugin-index-hash with size cap",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`safeHashFile` in `src/plugins/installed-plugin-index-hash.ts` reads entire files synchronously with no size limit — despite being named \"safe\". Plugin install records can reference arbitrarily large files (binaries, model files, bundled assets). A multi-GB `readFileSync` would OOM the Node process before the `catch` block can run.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nA function named \"safe\" should not have unbounded sync reads. The existing `catch` block handles ENOENT and permission errors but cannot prevent OOM from multi-GB files.\n\n## What Changed\n\nReplaced the hard 50 MiB rejection (from the original PR draft) with **bounded-memory streaming SHA-256 hashing**:\n\n- Files ≤ 50 MiB: read and hash in one call (unchanged behavior)\n- Files > 50 MiB: streamed in 64 KiB chunks using `fs.openSync` + `fs.readSync`, stopping after 50 MiB. This preserves a content hash for existing large files while keeping memory usage bounded.\n\nThe `statSync` pre-check still validates regular files and rejects non-regular paths before any read.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**All 27 tests pass:**\n\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.plugins.config.ts\n\n RUN  v4.1.10 /home/0668000387/openclawCxbAsDev\n\n ✓ |plugins| src/plugins/installed-plugin-index.test.ts (27 tests) 1115ms\n     ✓ drops blocked install record keys while reading persisted index records  426ms\n     ✓ discovers installed plugin packages from persisted install records  389ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  27 passed (27)\n   Start at  10:03:47\n   Duration  6.31s (transform 4.47s, setup 1.49s, import 3.34s, tests 1.11s, environment 0ms)\n\n## Changes\n\n- `src/plugins/installed-plugin-index-hash.ts`: Replace hard size rejection with streaming SHA-256 via `fs.openSync`/`fs.readSync` in 64 KiB chunks\n- `src/plugins/installed-plugin-index.test.ts`: Add regression test for streaming hash on files > 50 MiB",
        "branch": "fix/bound-plugin-index-hash",
